You don't need to worry about the speed vs temp parameters, the overall
design is supposed to work worst-case without having to derate the system,
if that's what you meant. (Plus, that worst case is over all possible
production variations, plus test equipment measurement error, plus the max
supply deviation.)

The part you are replacing was only rated 0-70 anyway, and all the post-74F
logic familys (e.g., ABT) use a lot less power and hence run cooler.

	ross

